# Anatomy illustration — version 2

Created with the built-in image-generation tool. Output: `anatomy-engraved-v2.png` (1024 × 1536 PNG with alpha).

The two user-supplied images were used as references: the full-body anatomical figure for composition, and the red ink-drawn heart for the organs' illustration style. Original user attachments were not changed.

## Generation prompt

Use case: style-transfer / scientific-educational. Create one polished website anatomy illustration by redrawing the human figure from Image 1 in the hand-engraved medical illustration style of Image 2. Input Image 1 is the composition/anatomy reference; Image 2 is the organ drawing STYLE reference, especially its black ink outlines, intricate fine hatching, arterial details and rich coral-red and blue-grey colors. Remove ALL of Image 1's typography, callout lines, glow, blue background, sparkles and interface ornaments. Output one isolated full-length human figure on genuinely transparent background, portrait 2:3 canvas, whole head and both feet visible, body centered, roughly 85% canvas height, generous clear margin. Front-facing neutral adult anatomical figure with arms slightly away from sides. Keep the body's outer form quiet and ghostlike, very pale sage-grey translucent skin and delicate engraved contours, subtle skeletal details, no scary skull face and no exposed genitals. Inside the intact pale figure show clean, beautiful detailed individually distinguishable colored organs: brain visible through cranium, both lungs with bronchi, warm red anatomical heart visible prominently between lungs slightly to viewer right, reddish brown liver beneath chest, softly muted digestive system below. Face has visible eyes and ears. All organs share Image 2's sharp fine black ink contours and rich hand-colored woodcut/etching crosshatching; they must NOT be childish clipart, flat icons, photoreal surgery, gross or gory. Heart in particular should match the supplied richly ink-drawn heart style. Anatomically plausible placement, proportional head/torso/legs, all organs inside silhouette, clean edges, no surrounding detached organs, no text, no labels, no border, no background color. This will be placed on warm ivory paper and receive live HTML labels and clickable organ hotspots.

## Integration

The illustration is decorative navigation, not a medical teaching reference. Visible labels and interactive links are live HTML, not baked into the image. The original generated image is also retained in the local Codex generated-images folder.

